Yes. I’d make it a first-class Ink Layer, not merely a screenshot hack. Copy this into the repo as the architecture/spec pseudocode.

MODULE: ChatInkLayer
PURPOSE:
    Allow the user to draw directly over/alongside a chat conversation.
    Preserve strokes as structured semantic input rather than flattening
    everything immediately into an image.
CORE PRINCIPLE:
    ink ≠ image attachment
    Ink is its own input modality:
        text
        voice
        image
        file
        ink
    Preserve BOTH:
        1. human-visible drawing
        2. machine-readable geometry + anchors
DATA TYPES
==========
TYPE Point:
    x: Float
    y: Float
    pressure: Float?
    tilt: Vector?
    timestamp: Time
TYPE StrokeStyle:
    tool: PEN | PENCIL | HIGHLIGHTER | ERASER
    width: Float
    color: Color
    opacity: Float
TYPE Stroke:
    id: UUID
    points: List<Point>
    style: StrokeStyle
TYPE ChatAnchor:
    message_id: UUID
    content_range: TextRange?       // optional words/characters
    bounding_box: Rect?             // rendered location when created
TYPE InkObject:
    id: UUID
    strokes: List<Stroke>
    // What was the drawing attached to?
    anchors: List<ChatAnchor>
    // Coordinate system prevents scrolling/layout changes
    // from destroying meaning.
    coordinate_space:
        MESSAGE_LOCAL |
        CANVAS_LOCAL |
        DOCUMENT_GLOBAL
    created_at: Time
    modified_at: Time
    semantic_state:
        RAW |
        INTERPRETED |
        CONFIRMED |
        SUPERSEDED
    interpretation: InkMeaning?
TYPE InkMeaning:
    primitives:
        ARROW
        CIRCLE
        UNDERLINE
        STRIKEOUT
        BRACKET
        CONNECTOR
        HANDWRITING
        FREEFORM_SKETCH
        REGION
        UNKNOWN
    referenced_objects: List<Reference>
    handwriting_text: String?
    inferred_relation:
        CONNECTS |
        CONTRASTS |
        GROUPS |
        EMPHASIZES |
        DELETES |
        MOVES |
        QUESTIONS |
        LABELS |
        CUSTOM
    confidence: Float
INTERACTION MODEL
=================
ON user_taps_draw_button:
    enter INK_MODE
    freeze semantic layout anchors
    overlay transparent InkCanvas on conversation
    allow:
        draw
        erase
        undo
        redo
        select
        move
        resize
        change color
        exit
ON pointer_down(event):
    stroke = Stroke(
        id = uuid(),
        style = current_tool,
        points = []
    )
    capture_pointer()
ON pointer_move(event):
    point = normalize(event)
    stroke.points.append(point)
    render_incrementally(stroke)
ON pointer_up(event):
    simplify_geometry(stroke)
    nearby_content =
        hit_test_chat_content(stroke.bounding_box)
    anchors =
        infer_anchors(stroke, nearby_content)
    InkObject.add(stroke, anchors)
    schedule_semantic_interpretation()
ANCHORING
=========
IMPORTANT:
    Never store meaning solely as screen coordinates.
EXAMPLE:
    User circles:
        "transfer the invariant intent/state"
    BAD:
        circle = [(412, 818), ...]
    GOOD:
        circle.geometry = [...]
        circle.anchor.message_id = "msg_8472"
        circle.anchor.content_range =
            chars(193..228)
THEN:
    if device rotates
    OR font size changes
    OR message reflows
    OR earlier content changes:
        resolve(anchor)
        transform(stroke_geometry)
        redraw_relative_to_anchor)
SEMANTIC INTERPRETATION
=======================
FUNCTION interpret_ink(ink, conversation):
    geometry_features =
        analyze_geometry(ink.strokes)
    spatial_targets =
        resolve_nearby_chat_elements(ink)
    handwriting =
        recognize_handwriting_if_present(ink)
    candidate_meanings =
        multimodal_model(
            conversation_context,
            rendered_region,
            geometry_features,
            handwriting,
            anchors
        )
    RETURN confidence_rank(candidate_meanings)
EXAMPLES:
    circle(text)
        -> EMPHASIZES(text)
    strike_through(text)
        -> PROPOSE_DELETE(text)
    arrow(A -> B)
        -> CONNECTS(A, B)
    handwritten "why?"
        + arrow to paragraph
        -> QUESTION(target=paragraph)
    bracket around messages 4-7
        -> GROUP(messages 4..7)
    draw box between two concepts
        -> POSSIBLE_NEW_OBJECT
    handwritten replacement above word
        -> PROPOSE_REPLACE(old, new)
    diagram in blank space
        -> FREEFORM_SKETCH
MODEL INPUT
===========
WHEN user presses SEND:
    packet = MultimodalTurn()
    packet.text =
        current_text_input
    packet.ink =
        serialize_structured_ink()
    packet.visual_context =
        render_only_regions_needed_for_interpretation()
    packet.references =
        resolve_all_ink_anchors()
    SEND packet
MODEL SHOULD RECEIVE SOMETHING LIKE:
{
    "user_text": "this relationship here",
    "ink": [
        {
            "type": "arrow",
            "from": {
                "message": 18,
                "text": "invariant intent"
            },
            "to": {
                "message": 21,
                "text": "shared representation"
            },
            "confidence": 0.96
        }
    ]
}
NOT merely:
    attachment = screenshot.png
MODEL RESPONSE BEHAVIOR
=======================
IF interpretation confidence >= HIGH:
    respond using inferred ink semantics
ELSE IF confidence >= MEDIUM:
    preserve multiple hypotheses
    example:
        "I read that arrow as connecting X to Y..."
ELSE:
    ask user what the mark denotes
NEVER silently convert uncertain handwriting
into a high-confidence instruction.
INLINE MANIPULATION
===================
Ink can also become an editing language.
GESTURE:
    circle paragraph + write "shorter"
TRANSLATE:
    EditIntent(
        target = paragraph,
        operation = COMPRESS
    )
GESTURE:
    strike paragraph
TRANSLATE:
    EditIntent(
        target = paragraph,
        operation = DELETE
    )
GESTURE:
    arrow paragraph A -> position after paragraph C
TRANSLATE:
    EditIntent(
        target = A,
        operation = MOVE,
        destination = after(C)
    )
GESTURE:
    circle two ideas + write "="
TRANSLATE:
    SemanticIntent(
        operation = COMPARE_OR_UNIFY,
        objects = [A, B]
    )
SELECTION / LASSO
=================
ON lasso(region):
    objects =
        select(
            ink_strokes,
            messages,
            images,
            diagrams
            intersecting region
        )
    show_context_actions:
        ASK_ABOUT
        COPY
        DELETE_INK
        GROUP
        MOVE
        EXTRACT
        EXPLAIN
        TRANSFORM
IMAGE ANNOTATION
================
IF ink overlaps image:
    anchor strokes to:
        image_id
        normalized image coordinates
    Example:
        user circles bird in photo
        model receives:
            image_id
            polygon
            instruction/context
    This enables:
        "what is this?"
        "remove this"
        "make this red"
        "identify this plant"
        "look specifically here"
PERSISTENCE
===========
STORE:
    original_strokes
    semantic interpretation
    anchors
    transformations
    conversation version
DO NOT destructively rasterize.
Rasterization is merely a VIEW.
Canonical representation remains:
    vector ink
        +
    semantic anchors
        +
    conversation state
DELTA / LEARNING LOOP
=====================
After model response:
    compare:
        inferred_ink_meaning
        vs
        subsequent_user_behavior
    IF user corrects interpretation:
        record semantic_delta
        update:
            gesture model
            user-specific conventions
EXAMPLE:
    repeated spiral around concept
        eventually learns:
            user means "recurse/explore this"
BUT:
    learned gestures remain inspectable
    and reversible.
EXTENSION: SHARED WHITEBOARD
============================
Eventually:
    ChatInkLayer
        -> InfiniteCanvas
where:
    messages
    images
    files
    model outputs
    drawings
    diagrams
    generated objects
become movable nodes.
User can physically arrange thought:
    [idea A] ----arrow----> [idea B]
       |                       |
       v                       v
    [photo]                 [paper]
       \                       /
        ------> [new synthesis]
Model observes:
    CONTENT
    +
    GEOMETRY
    +
    RELATIONSHIPS
    +
    TEMPORAL EDIT HISTORY
Thus spatial arrangement itself becomes language.
MINIMUM VIABLE VERSION
======================
V0:
    transparent drawing overlay
    pen / highlighter / eraser
    undo
    screenshot sent with message
V1:
    vector stroke persistence
    message-relative anchors
V2:
    arrow/circle/underline detection
    handwriting recognition
    structured model input
V3:
    ink gestures operate on chat objects
V4:
    movable messages/images/files
    spatial canvas
V5:
    persistent multimodal workspace
    where ink + language + spatial arrangement
    are equivalent first-class interfaces.
INVARIANT
=========
NEVER reduce a rich input modality earlier than necessary.
stroke
    -> geometry
    -> spatial relationship
    -> semantic hypothesis
    -> intent
    -> action
Only rasterize when a downstream interface
cannot consume the richer representation.

The key architectural decision is anchored vector ink. If we merely put a transparent drawing surface over chat and submit screenshots, we’ve recreated Notes with extra steps. If the system knows what you circled, where an arrow begins and ends, and which message a handwritten annotation belongs to, drawing becomes a second grammar for talking to the model.

And that fits our existing representation work almost perfectly: preserve the richest representation upstream, then compile it down only when a downstream substrate requires it.